# GitHub workflow safety

- Use least-privilege workflow permissions and never expose secrets to fork
  pull requests.
- Keep deterministic checks (`quality`, `e2e`, `rls`) independently runnable;
  do not make the advisory AI reviewer a required merge gate without a proven
  lifecycle.
- Do not weaken branch protections, RLS checks, artifact redaction, or secret
  handling to make CI pass.
- Pin action versions and document any new external permission or secret in the
  related pull request.
